.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="RedoxTitration computes the electrode potential during a redox titration from the Nernst equation, E=E^\circ-\frac{RT}{nF}\ln Q: before equivalence the analyte couple sets E, after it the titrant couple does. At half-equivalence E=E^\circ_1 exactly, at twice the equivalence volume E=E^\circ_2, and the endpoint is read, as in the laboratory, at the steepest rise of E.">

